Gorm persistence callback and JSON serializer compatibility references

Copyright (c) 2013-present Jinzhu <wosmvp@gmail.com>

Native JSON nil-to-SQL-NULL and HTML-safe JSON behavior follows
schema/serializer.go. Fresh captured belongs-to saves, ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING,
auto timestamps and selected struct-update semantics follow
callbacks/associations.go, callbacks/callbacks.go, callbacks/create.go and
callbacks/update.go. Ordinary nullable bool zero-value scans follow
schema/field.go and scan.go from gorm.io/gorm v1.31.1, used by the pinned headscale-go
v0.29.5 persistence path. The implementation is maintained in Rust; no Gorm
runtime dependency is introduced. The original MIT terms are retained in
LICENSE-GORM.

